    "multi_column_TbzGnm": {
      "type": "multi-column",
      "blocks": {
        "item_qkyprL": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "icon_width": 32,
            "icon_background_type": "square",
            "icon_background": "",
            "icon_color": "",
            "background_color": "#3e4650",
            "text_color": "",
            "border_color": "#696969",
            "show_controls": false,
            "column_size": "1",
            "title": "",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "subheading": "",
            "content": "<h5>Store Managers: Daily Performance Checks</h5><p>Store managers began checking Flow dashboards each morning to understand yesterday's performance and throughout the day to monitor real-time traffic. This became part of the daily routine within the first month of deployment.</p><p>✅ 92% of managers reported daily dashboard usage after 3 months</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_YXkcqb": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "icon_width": 32,
            "icon_background_type": "square",
            "icon_background": "",
            "icon_color": "",
            "background_color": "#3e4650",
            "text_color": "",
            "border_color": "#696969",
            "show_controls": false,
            "column_size": "1",
            "title": "",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "subheading": "",
            "content": "<h5>Earlier Issue Identification</h5><p>Managers could identify problems during the day rather than discovering them in end-of-day sales reports. For example, seeing high traffic but low conversion during lunch hours prompted immediate staffing adjustments.</p><p>✅ Average response time to issues decreased from next-day to same-day</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_CtDYAK": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "icon_width": 32,
            "icon_background_type": "square",
            "icon_background": "",
            "icon_color": "",
            "background_color": "#3e4650",
            "text_color": "",
            "border_color": "#696969",
            "show_controls": false,
            "column_size": "1",
            "title": "",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "subheading": "",
            "content": "<h5>Mid-Week Staffing Adjustments</h5><p>Instead of fixed weekly schedules, managers began making mid-week adjustments based on observed traffic patterns. Slow Monday mornings led to reduced staff, while unexpected Wednesday peaks triggered additional coverage.</p><p>✅ Staff schedule flexibility increased significantly</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_Wgc6iW": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "icon_width": 32,
            "icon_background_type": "square",
            "icon_background": "",
            "icon_color": "",
            "background_color": "#3e4650",
            "text_color": "",
            "border_color": "#696969",
            "show_controls": false,
            "column_size": "1",
            "title": "",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "subheading": "",
            "content": "<h5>Data-Validated Assumptions</h5><p>Managers could test assumptions about what drove traffic. For example, one store believed rainy weather hurt traffic, but Flow data showed traffic was consistent—conversion dropped instead, suggesting an in-store service issue.</p><p>✅ Shifted decision-making from intuition to evidence</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        },
        "item_RKiW9c": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "icon_width": 32,
            "icon_background_type": "square",
            "icon_background": "",
            "icon_color": "",
            "background_color": "#3e4650",
            "text_color": "",
            "border_color": "#696969",
            "show_controls": false,
            "column_size": "1",
            "title": "",
            "heading_tag": "h4",
            "subheading": "",
            "content": "<h5>Increased Manager Confidence</h5><p>Store managers reported feeling more confident in performance discussions with area supervisors. Having concrete traffic and conversion data reduced uncertainty and enabled more productive conversations about improvement strategies.</p><p>✅ Improved communication quality between store and HQ</p>",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_style": "link"
          }
        }
      },
